{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792894319,"nonce":"eRZSwWcuXciVhJ8ToPO5fo0ncp0=","title":"Snapshot cache: concurrent publication fails on Windows with Access is denied","message":"`snapshot::cache::tests::concurrent_publishers_do_not_expose_partial_snapshots` fails on x86_64-pc-windows-msvc (Rust CI run 40149017133, main 39cdefea). Each of the three publisher threads panics at `cache.store(...).unwrap()` with `Encode(\"Access is denied. (os error 5)\")`.\n\n`persist_cancellable` writes a `NamedTempFile` and renames it over the cache path. On Windows that rename (MoveFileEx with replace) is refused while another handle has the target open without FILE_SHARE_DELETE, and `load` holds one through `std::fs::read`; two publishers renaming over the same target can also collide. On Unix the rename replaces the directory entry and readers keep the old inode, so the test passes there.\n\nEarlier Windows jobs stopped at a failing zynml test before reaching zyntax_embed, so this is the first run to show it; the code came in with 585f0992.\n\nA publication that loses to a reader or another publisher could retry briefly on PermissionDenied and then give up without error, since the cache is only an accelerator and a concurrent publisher is writing an equivalent artifact.","files":null}]}